WEBVTT

00:00:00.282 --> 00:00:01.690
Last video ended here.

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:04.498
The integral of sine x, from zero to

00:00:04.558 --> 00:00:07.366
two pi, is zero, because the arch below

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:09.272
the axis cancels the arch above.

00:00:10.114 --> 00:00:12.522
Picture sine t as the velocity of a

00:00:12.623 --> 00:00:15.452
lift, in floors per second, over two pi

00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:15.854
seconds.

00:00:16.557 --> 00:00:18.426
For the first half, it rises two floors.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.584
For the second half, it comes back down

00:00:20.645 --> 00:00:20.826
two.

00:00:21.471 --> 00:00:23.236
It ends where it started, so its net

00:00:23.277 --> 00:00:24.319
change is zero.

00:00:24.942 --> 00:00:27.326
But it still travelled four floors, and the

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:30.092
shaded region has area four, two for each

00:00:30.213 --> 00:00:30.413
arch.

00:00:31.196 --> 00:00:34.074
The integral keeps signs, and the area doesn't.

00:00:34.777 --> 00:00:37.684
So how do signed integrals differ from total

00:00:37.826 --> 00:00:40.151
area, and how do we find the area

00:00:40.293 --> 00:00:42.057
when part of the region is below the

00:00:42.158 --> 00:00:42.458
axis?

00:00:43.048 --> 00:00:44.355
Start with the easy case.

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:47.245
When the curve stays on or above the

00:00:47.327 --> 00:00:47.667
axis,

00:00:48.189 --> 00:00:50.978
every strip has a positive height, so every

00:00:51.039 --> 00:00:51.941
strip adds area.

00:00:52.845 --> 00:00:54.951
Then the area and the integral are the

00:00:55.012 --> 00:00:55.633
same number.

00:00:56.337 --> 00:00:56.537
Take

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:59.953
y equals two x plus one, from one

00:01:00.054 --> 00:01:00.495
to three.

00:01:01.359 --> 00:01:04.667
Earlier, we found this trapezium's area, ten, by

00:01:04.708 --> 00:01:05.188
geometry.

00:01:05.931 --> 00:01:06.772
Now with a primitive,

00:01:07.435 --> 00:01:10.481
x squared plus x, it's twelve minus two,

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:11.263
which is ten.

00:01:12.007 --> 00:01:14.663
Same number, because nothing is below the axis.

00:01:15.435 --> 00:01:17.042
Now a region below the axis.

00:01:17.506 --> 00:01:20.198
Take y equals x squared minus four, from

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:21.002
zero to two.

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:23.652
On this stretch the curve is under the

00:01:23.754 --> 00:01:26.321
axis, so every height is negative, and every

00:01:26.403 --> 00:01:27.907
strip adds a negative amount.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.538
A primitive is x cubed over three, minus

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:32.160
four x.

00:01:32.803 --> 00:01:35.207
At two that's eight thirds minus eight, which

00:01:35.268 --> 00:01:37.813
is minus sixteen thirds, and at zero it's

00:01:37.954 --> 00:01:38.274
zero.

00:01:38.897 --> 00:01:41.223
So the integral is minus sixteen thirds.

00:01:41.906 --> 00:01:43.562
But an area can't be negative.

00:01:44.288 --> 00:01:46.879
A strip's area uses its length, and here

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:48.447
the length is minus the height.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.699
So the area is the integral with its

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:52.649
sign removed, sixteen thirds.

00:01:53.334 --> 00:01:55.342
We write it as the absolute value of

00:01:55.383 --> 00:01:57.692
the integral, or as minus the integral.

00:01:58.221 --> 00:02:00.309
What happens when the curve crosses the axis?

00:02:01.113 --> 00:02:02.887
Stretch the same curve out to three.

00:02:03.512 --> 00:02:05.497
It crosses at two, and from two to

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:06.801
three it's above the axis.

00:02:07.444 --> 00:02:09.321
That piece has integral seven thirds.

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:12.200
Now the whole integral, from zero to three,

00:02:12.602 --> 00:02:13.386
is minus three.

00:02:13.909 --> 00:02:16.564
And minus three is seven thirds, minus sixteen

00:02:16.604 --> 00:02:16.886
thirds.

00:02:17.711 --> 00:02:19.841
So the integral is the area above the

00:02:19.943 --> 00:02:21.771
axis, minus the area below it.

00:02:22.354 --> 00:02:25.181
That's the lift's net change, floors up minus

00:02:25.222 --> 00:02:25.742
floors down.

00:02:26.465 --> 00:02:27.651
But it's not the area.

00:02:28.417 --> 00:02:30.987
For the area, like the floors travelled, take

00:02:31.149 --> 00:02:32.795
each piece on its own and make it

00:02:32.856 --> 00:02:33.257
positive.

00:02:33.941 --> 00:02:36.877
Sixteen thirds plus seven thirds is twenty-three thirds.

00:02:37.662 --> 00:02:38.749
Often there's no graph.

00:02:39.532 --> 00:02:40.953
Find the area bounded by y

00:02:41.514 --> 00:02:44.138
equals x squared minus four x plus three,

00:02:44.538 --> 00:02:47.122
the x-axis, and the lines x equals zero

00:02:47.422 --> 00:02:48.343
and x equals four.

00:02:49.207 --> 00:02:51.325
First, find where the curve meets the axis.

00:02:51.967 --> 00:02:55.092
It factorises as x minus one, times x

00:02:55.153 --> 00:02:57.657
minus three, so the zeros are one and

00:02:57.717 --> 00:02:57.937
three.

00:02:58.681 --> 00:03:00.514
They split the interval into three pieces.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.578
Test a value in each piece.

00:03:03.243 --> 00:03:05.389
At zero, y is three, positive.

00:03:05.913 --> 00:03:08.389
At two, y is minus one, negative.

00:03:08.953 --> 00:03:11.263
At four, y is three, positive.

00:03:12.006 --> 00:03:13.332
Now integrate each piece.

00:03:13.814 --> 00:03:16.506
The answers are four thirds, minus four thirds,

00:03:16.749 --> 00:03:17.612
and four thirds.

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.528
Make each one positive and add, so the

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:21.493
area is four.

00:03:22.278 --> 00:03:24.345
The single integral from zero to four is

00:03:24.386 --> 00:03:27.035
only four thirds, because the middle piece cancels

00:03:27.157 --> 00:03:27.698
one of the others.

00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:30.254
The same method works for every function in

00:03:30.295 --> 00:03:30.675
the course.

00:03:31.279 --> 00:03:33.150
Take y equals e to the x, minus

00:03:33.211 --> 00:03:34.378
two, from zero to one.

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.465
It meets the axis where e to the

00:03:36.586 --> 00:03:38.772
x is two, so x is the natural

00:03:38.813 --> 00:03:41.039
log of two, about zero point six nine.

00:03:41.783 --> 00:03:44.193
At zero, y is minus one, so the

00:03:44.214 --> 00:03:45.761
first piece is below the axis.

00:03:46.465 --> 00:03:46.865
At one,

00:03:47.408 --> 00:03:49.575
y is e minus two, which is positive.

00:03:50.377 --> 00:03:52.199
With the primitive e to the x minus

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:55.184
two x, the first piece is one, minus

00:03:55.265 --> 00:03:57.247
two times the natural log of two, which

00:03:57.309 --> 00:03:57.768
is negative.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.836
The second is e minus four, plus two

00:04:00.877 --> 00:04:01.999
times the natural log of two.

00:04:02.684 --> 00:04:04.397
Make the first one positive and add.

00:04:04.862 --> 00:04:07.751
The area is e minus five, plus four

00:04:07.793 --> 00:04:09.036
times the natural log of two,

00:04:09.559 --> 00:04:10.822
about zero point four nine.

00:04:11.426 --> 00:04:13.395
Keep the log exact all the way through,

00:04:13.718 --> 00:04:15.064
and round only at the end.

00:04:15.756 --> 00:04:17.949
This difference has a meaning when the graph

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:18.633
is a velocity.

00:04:19.297 --> 00:04:21.521
Take the car with velocity twelve minus two

00:04:21.622 --> 00:04:23.886
t metres per second, from zero to eight

00:04:23.927 --> 00:04:24.247
seconds.

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:26.757
Its integral is thirty-two metres.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.732
That's the displacement, where the car ends up

00:04:29.794 --> 00:04:30.899
compared with where it started.

00:04:31.543 --> 00:04:33.395
But the car stops at six seconds and

00:04:33.416 --> 00:04:34.060
then reverses.

00:04:34.845 --> 00:04:37.252
Forward from zero to six, it travels thirty-six

00:04:37.294 --> 00:04:37.554
metres.

00:04:38.036 --> 00:04:40.081
From six to eight, the integral is minus

00:04:40.142 --> 00:04:42.126
four, so it travels four metres back.

00:04:42.850 --> 00:04:45.543
The total distance is thirty-six plus four, which

00:04:45.604 --> 00:04:46.427
is forty metres.

00:04:47.132 --> 00:04:48.821
Displacement is the signed integral.

00:04:49.284 --> 00:04:50.690
Distance is the area.

00:04:51.463 --> 00:04:52.659
Here's a way to remember the method.

00:04:53.363 --> 00:04:54.184
Find the zeros,

00:04:54.865 --> 00:04:55.206
split,

00:04:55.907 --> 00:04:56.708
flip the negatives,

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:57.750
then add.

00:04:58.532 --> 00:04:59.962
The integral keeps the signs.

00:05:00.505 --> 00:05:02.798
The area makes every piece positive.

00:05:05.376 --> 00:05:05.780
Your turn.

00:05:06.345 --> 00:05:08.428
Find the area of the region bounded by

00:05:08.789 --> 00:05:11.513
y equals x times x minus two, the

00:05:11.694 --> 00:05:14.538
x-axis, and the lines x equals zero and

00:05:14.759 --> 00:05:15.559
x equals four.

00:05:16.184 --> 00:05:17.150
Pause here to answer.

00:05:27.736 --> 00:05:29.653
The zeros are zero and two.

00:05:30.258 --> 00:05:32.266
From zero to two, the curve is below

00:05:32.327 --> 00:05:34.335
the axis, and the integral is minus four

00:05:34.396 --> 00:05:34.736
thirds.

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.272
From two to four, it's above, and the

00:05:37.293 --> 00:05:38.601
integral is twenty thirds.

00:05:39.225 --> 00:05:40.652
Make both positive and add.

00:05:41.357 --> 00:05:44.311
Four thirds plus twenty thirds is twenty-four thirds,

00:05:44.493 --> 00:05:45.055
which is eight.

00:05:45.821 --> 00:05:46.887
Sixteen thirds is wrong.

00:05:47.331 --> 00:05:49.363
That's the signed integral, where the piece below

00:05:49.384 --> 00:05:50.590
the axis subtracts.

00:05:52.376 --> 00:05:52.859
Last one.

00:05:53.705 --> 00:05:55.871
The graph shows y equals f of x,

00:05:56.153 --> 00:05:57.436
from zero to six.

00:05:58.099 --> 00:06:00.125
The region from zero to two is above

00:06:00.186 --> 00:06:01.810
the axis, with area five.

00:06:02.493 --> 00:06:04.344
The region from two to six is below

00:06:04.405 --> 00:06:05.913
the axis, with area three.

00:06:06.778 --> 00:06:08.743
Find the integral from zero to six of

00:06:09.025 --> 00:06:10.649
f, and the total area.

00:06:11.476 --> 00:06:12.346
Pause here to answer.

00:06:23.201 --> 00:06:25.547
The integral counts the region below the axis

00:06:25.667 --> 00:06:28.274
as negative, so it's five minus three, which

00:06:28.314 --> 00:06:28.695
is two.

00:06:29.437 --> 00:06:32.200
The total area counts both as positive, so

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:34.062
it's five plus three, which is eight.

00:06:35.025 --> 00:06:36.302
Eight for the integral is wrong.

00:06:36.867 --> 00:06:38.956
It treats the region below the axis as

00:06:39.036 --> 00:06:39.679
if it were above.

00:06:41.335 --> 00:06:44.040
So the integral is above minus below, and

00:06:44.061 --> 00:06:46.326
the area adds every piece as positive.

00:06:47.271 --> 00:06:49.043
Every region so far has sat against the

00:06:49.185 --> 00:06:49.647
x-axis.

00:06:50.211 --> 00:06:50.871
Here's a different one:

00:06:51.432 --> 00:06:53.893
the region between y equals the natural log

00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:56.435
of x, the y-axis, and the lines y

00:06:56.676 --> 00:06:58.717
equals zero and y equals one.

00:07:00.141 --> 00:07:02.148
Our strips stood up from the x-axis.

00:07:02.692 --> 00:07:04.205
Here, they'd have to lie sideways.

00:07:04.933 --> 00:07:06.286
So how do we find this area?

00:07:09.335 --> 00:07:10.137
Here are the key notes.

00:07:10.781 --> 00:07:12.508
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:13.051
to copy them.
